sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Although inferring the generating procedure from observed behavior is fairly easy for the rules of traditional mathematics, for general simple programs it is often extremely difficult, because their complex output shows no obvious trace of its simple origin.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recovering a simple rule from its complex output is usually very hard";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 10, “Processes of Perception and Analysis”; section “What Perception and Analysis Do” (from p. 548), p. 550. Scope: inference of generating rules from the output of cellular automata and other simple programs"
}
